From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DolphinSlicer <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Arachne: interpolate() must not depend on the width of
 size_t

SkeletalTrapezoidation::interpolate(left, ratio, right, switching_radius)
starts its search at coord_t(left.toolpath_locations.size() - 1). For an
empty vector the unsigned subtraction wraps; with a 64-bit size_t the
conversion to the 64-bit coord_t gives -1 and the loop is skipped, but
with a 32-bit size_t (WebAssembly wasm32, other 32-bit targets) it gives
4294967295 and the loop reads toolpath_locations[2^32 - 1], far out of
bounds ("memory access out of bounds" in WebAssembly; seen slicing a
finely tessellated sphere and reported by OrcaWeb for the Voron Design
Cube and the Stanford Bunny).

Convert to coord_t before subtracting. Behaviour on 64-bit platforms is
unchanged.

Upstreamable: yes (32-bit portability).
---
 src/libslic3r/Arachne/SkeletalTrapezoidation.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Arachne/SkeletalTrapezoidation.cpp b/src/libslic3r/Arachne/SkeletalTrapezoidation.cpp
index 077ffd1a..72903148 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/Arachne/SkeletalTrapezoidation.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Arachne/SkeletalTrapezoidation.cpp
@@ -1676,7 +1676,9 @@ SkeletalTrapezoidation::Beading SkeletalTrapezoidation::interpolate(const Beadin
     // TODO: don't use toolpath locations past the middle!
     // TODO: stretch bead widths and locations of the higher bead count beading to fit in the left over space
     coord_t next_inset_idx;
-    for (next_inset_idx = left.toolpath_locations.size() - 1; next_inset_idx >= 0; next_inset_idx--)
+    // Convert before subtracting: with an empty vector, size() - 1 wraps around, and only a
+    // 64-bit size_t wraps to -1 when converted to coord_t (with a 32-bit size_t it becomes 2^32-1).
+    for (next_inset_idx = coord_t(left.toolpath_locations.size()) - 1; next_inset_idx >= 0; next_inset_idx--)
     {
         if (switching_radius > left.toolpath_locations[next_inset_idx])
         {
